	"data": "Georgia Tech — MS-HCI & GVU Center\n\nPart of [[projects/grad-school-options|Grad School Options]] research.\n\nOverview\n\nGeorgia Tech's Master of Science in Human-Computer Interaction (MS-HCI) is one of the oldest and most established interdisciplinary HCI programs in the United States. Created in 1998, it spans four schools — Interactive Computing, Literature, Media & Communication (LMC), Industrial Design, and Psychology — offering students a uniquely broad perspective on human-computer…",
